= Solution
{c}
{parent=a}

For every tuple of parameters $\bar a\in M^n$, a <downward absolute formula> transfers truth from the larger structure to the smaller one:
$$
\boxed{(N,\in)\models\varphi(\bar a)\quad\Longrightarrow\quad(M,\in)\models\varphi(\bar a).}
$$
The condition concerns every parameter tuple from $M$, not merely parameter-free sentences.

= b
{parent=iv}
{scope}

= Solution
{c}
{parent=b}

For every tuple of parameters $\bar a\in M^n$, an <upward absolute formula> transfers truth from the smaller structure to the larger one:
$$
\boxed{(M,\in)\models\varphi(\bar a)\quad\Longrightarrow\quad(N,\in)\models\varphi(\bar a).}
$$
These definitions of directional <set-theoretic absoluteness> do not themselves require the structures to be transitive.

= c
{parent=iv}
{scope}

= Solution
{c}
{parent=c}

A formula has <set-theoretic absoluteness> between these structures when both directions hold for every $\bar a\in M^n$:
$$
\boxed{(M,\in)\models\varphi(\bar a)\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad(N,\in)\models\varphi(\bar a).}
$$
Equivalently, it is both a <downward absolute formula> and an <upward absolute formula> between them.

= v
{parent=1}
